From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caboose <caboose@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/31] Report device loss at every encoder call after the
 executor left

Once the executor is gone, a reply read on the ended stream reads as
VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST in every word, which is right for a call's result but
leaves garbage in its other outputs (handles, counts, sizes) that ANGLE used
before checking for loss, crashing Chromium's GPU process. Every encoder call
now returns VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST (or nothing) at entry instead, without
touching its outputs (caboose-bounded-memory/completion_feed.h lostCall).
---
 .../vulkan_enc/autogenerated/VkEncoder.cpp    | 720 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 720 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/autogenerated/VkEncoder.cpp b/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/autogenerated/VkEncoder.cpp
index e585446..04f94ff 100644
